1
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:39,540
Thank you for allowing me
to meditate with you.

2
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:44,700
This is normally done
in private, counselor...

3
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:49,460
...but it is an honor to teach Vulcan
techniques to one so willing.

4
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:58,440
These sessions... They're the only times
that Vulcans pay attention to their emotions?

5
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:06,260
We find it salutary to have an interval during
which we ask ourselves the question
no other Vulcan may:

6
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,880
"How do you feel?"

7
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,640
When this mission is over...

8
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,700
I will miss these times with you.

9
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:28,940
And I with you.

10
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:34,180
Doctor, I believe you may benefit from

11
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:36,760
further teaching with masters on Vulcan.

12
00:01:38,550 --> 00:01:40,100
Perhaps you could as well.

13
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:44,200
There's a discipline called
the "Dalhutnar," isn't there?

14
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:48,920
To help one accept the wisdom
of vestigial emotions.

15
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:53,670
There is also the "Kolinahr":
the purging of all remaining emotions.

16
00:01:55,670 --> 00:02:00,120
There is no chance of me undertaking
the former, nor the latter.

17
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,680
I am rarely disposed to discuss
matters of a private nature...

18
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:15,120
but our relationship is... special.

19
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:24,840
I have served aboard this starship for
sixteen years under two captains.

20
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,820
I would not admit this in front of Dr. McCoy...

21
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:35,700
but such a lengthy association with

22
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:40,520
men and women from Earth has
taught me to value

23
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:49,080
my maternal birthright in a way I never
could had I remained on Vulcan.

24
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:13,020
KIRK (VO):
Captain's log, stardate 6988.4. The Enterprise
is scheduled to return to Earth shortly.

25
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:20,480
I always intended to bring her back in one
piece, but the triumph is bittersweet.

26
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:26,280
The recent loss of our
sister ship still gnaws at me.

27
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:35,100
Whatever it was that caused the Hood's
crew to lose life support, killing all 430
men and women aboard is...

28
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:38,310
[INTERCOM WHISTLES]

29
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,929
Kirk here.

30
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:46,240
UHURA:
Priority incoming message from
the Chief of Starfleet Operations.

31
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,060
I'll take it down here, lieutenant.

32
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:54,000
Admiral Thesp.

33
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,056
Captain... priority one. We're diverting you to Aldebaran.

34
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:05,320
Admiral, considering the ships we've lost in
that system recently, do you think that's wise?

35
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:13,040
Wise or not, it's necessary. The Yorktown
and Republic were severely damaged during their
investigation into the Hood's loss.

36
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:19,540
And shortly afterwards, the Federation colony
on Aldebaran III went completely silent.

37
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,640
How could an entire Federation
colony suddenly go silent?

38
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:29,580
Starfleet has a top-secret
laboratory on that world.

39
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:34,740
The supply vessel we sent to investigate --
the S.S. Halifax -- never returned.

40
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:41,900
Before we lost contact, the Halifax reported
significant anti-proton residue
on the planet's surface.

41
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,960
I think you know what that means.

42
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,120
Romulans.

43
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,920
KIRK (VO):
Space. The final frontier.

44
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:14,340
These are the voyages of the
Starship Enterprise.

45
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:16,836
Its continuing mission:

46
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,268
to explore strange
new worlds.

47
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:23,120
To seek out new life
and new civilizations.

48
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:26,940
To boldly go
where no man has gone before.

49
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:17,400
Captain, readings indicate the colony
has been destroyed.

50
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,040
Romulan plasma weapon?

51
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:25,660
Judging by the damage, it appears the central
reactor has suffered a containment failure.

52
00:06:25,850 --> 00:06:28,490
- That's unusual.
- It's impossible! I installed the
safeguards myself 5 years ago.

53
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,800
Perhaps some kind of sabotage.

54
00:06:31,014 --> 00:06:33,377
SCOTT:
At least the Pandora Science Lab's intact.

55
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:38,040
But it's underground -- and it generates a
particle scattering field. I'll have to put
ya down outside.

56
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,000
- Just put us down in one piece, Scotty.
- Aye sir.
- Energize.

57
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:19,460
The disruption field is
obstructing my readings.

58
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:29,860
I am detecting 2 life forms
large enough to be humanoid.

59
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:38,280
I don't suppose they left a key
under a rock somewhere.

60
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,960
I can attempt to access the lift using
standard Federation prefixes...

61
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:52,340
Automated defenses!

62
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:17,820
We must maintain the barrage!
The drone cannot fire through its own shields!

63
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:29,660
Spock! Sould the turret's anti-grav beam
be creating a gap on the bottom
of its deflector screen?

64
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:34,360
- Highly possible.
- Let's find out.

65
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,000
Fascinating.

66
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:55,560
LANA:
You're Vulcan.

67
00:08:57,860 --> 00:09:03,200
- You. You're Vulcan.
- Affirmative.

68
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:07,700
When a simple "yes" would do.
Vulcan for sure.

69
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:14,790
Forgive the attack. The drone's sensors
thought you were another Romulan invader.

70
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:19,280
The bio-signs are almost identical.
You're in charge?

71
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,820
Captain James T. Kirk.
Federation starship Enterprise.

72
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,640
"T" for Tiberius.

73
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:39,160
Who are you? What happened here?

74
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,280
You don't know?

75
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:48,880
It was your starship that first pierced
the barrier around our galaxy 5 years ago.

76
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:56,260
An energy field that enhances humans
with high ESP quotients. "Uplifts" them.

77
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:02,420
Since then, certain Starfleet officials
have been asembling us.

78
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:07,240
Testing us. Experimenting. 25 in total.

79
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:11,220
It appears you, too, have journeyed
through the barrier yourself.

80
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:15,740
- A trial run.
- Trial for what?

81
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,480
The ultimate last resort.

82
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,060
Protection against invasion.

83
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,200
In the event the Federation is
ever invaded by a superior force,

84
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,580
we were to fly through the
galactic barrier.

85
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:32,920
Granting you superior powers.
Effectively weaponizing you.

86
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,200
The Federation isn't in the business
of weaponizing its citizens.

87
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,620
You should better familiarize yourself
with the Starfleet charter.

88
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,960
Article 14, Section 31.

89
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:48,840
Captain. Absolute power does NOT
corrupt absolutely.

90
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,480
It corrupts SELECTIVELY...

91
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:54,440
...as you know from experience.

92
00:10:55,020 --> 00:11:01,460
Aboard your ship, one uplifted esper became
a megalomaniac... while the other retained humanity.

93
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,800
And which are you?

94
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:07,620
I follow "Sas-tar-po-harn."

95
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:14,980
A human spiritual movement that follows
the pacifist teachings of Surak
and T'Mord of Vulcan.

96
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:20,380
- Psychologically unsuitable espers were
excluded from this project.
- About my original question:

97
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,780
What happened here?

98
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:35,780
A cloaked vessel arrived. They overwhelmed the lab.
Destroyed the ship sent here to investigate.

99
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:37,300
The Halifax.

100
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:43,720
The Romulans vaporized our scientists
and kidnapped the espers.

101
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:45,680
What about you?

102
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:50,700
I used my powers to suspend my life signs.

103
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:56,160
I "played dead."

104
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,820
What do Romulans want with
a bunch of espers?

105
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,280
I believe I can surmise the answer, lieutenant.

106
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:08,160
Despite my advanced ESP rating, my
experiences with the barrier
failed to uplift me.

107
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:13,280
I suspect Vulcan physiology renders us
immune to the psionic effects.

108
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,960
- And, if Vulcans cannot be uplifted...
- Then neither can Romulans.

109
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:23,280
They want to use the kidnapped espers
to form an attack force.

110
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:27,140
But not against us, captain.
Against the Romulan Praetor.

111
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:30,240
They oppose his termination
of the Klingon alliance.

112
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,720
Romulan politics don't concern me.
Getting my people back does.

113
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,760
What's your name?

114
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:39,080
Lana.

115
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:41,353
You'll be safe with us, Lana.

116
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:43,662
SPOCK:
Captain, a word?

117
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:53,880
If you recall, it was incredibly dangerous
to have Mitchell aboard the Enterprise
after his powers had multiplied.

118
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:59,700
If we leave Lana here, she will remain
as we intended HIM to be:
Isolated, where she could do no harm.

119
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:01,900
You heard her Spock. She's a pacifist.

120
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:05,900
Besides, if we're going to pursue a
Romulan ship full of espers --

121
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:09,740
espers that've been turned --
I want us to have one of our own.

122
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,510
A most logical position.

123
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,280
You sound surprised.

124
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:19,660
Captain, there is the matter of the
other life form I detected.

125
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:21,860
SENTEK:
That would be me, commander!

126
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,200
Drop your weapon!

127
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:30,640
Do you feel confident that you can
shoot me before I kill your captain?
Disarm NOW.

128
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,740
Hold your position, lieutenant!

129
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,880
Surrender is not the Romulan way, captain.

130
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:45,180
Fire now, and this disruptor will detonate.
I have no quarrel with you.

131
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:49,700
Save yourselves.
But the mutant stays with me.

132
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:56,220
Given that particular model of firearm, I
believe we have approximately 38 seconds
until a forced-chamber overload.

133
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,380
We will not abandon a Federation citizen!

134
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,680
It seems you have little choice.

135
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,530
[GRUNTS, FIGHTING]

136
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,340
- Kirk to Enterprise!
- Captain, we cannot leave him here to die.

137
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,120
Emergency! Five to beam out -- NOW!

138
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,810
[EXPLOSION]

139
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:53,320
Sulu has detected the Romulan kidnappers
on long-range sensors.

140
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:57,220
- We are on an intercept course.
- Excellent.

141
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:02,360
Admiral, I won't lie. They have a head start.
A good one.

142
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:06,160
They'll cross into the Neutral Zone before
we can catch them.

143
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,620
A week before my retirement.

144
00:15:12,130 --> 00:15:17,340
Captain, I'm ordering you to pursue those
"karskat" Romulans into the Zone...

145
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:26,520
...all the way to the home worlds if you have to.
Just get the espers back -- no matter what.
Starfleet out.

146
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:42,940
- Kirk to bridge.
- Spock here.

147
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:49,560
Set a course for the Romulan Neutral Zone.
Maximum warp.

148
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:55,640
Acknowledged.

149
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:57,620
Mr. Spock?

150
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:03,100
- You heard the order lieutenant.
- Yes, sir.

151
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:08,920
Uhura, transmit this encrypted message
on the following subspace frequency.

152
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,400
- Sir, that carrier wave is only used...
- Please proceed.

153
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,420
Direct any response to my quarters.

154
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:30,600
Four-oh. Perfect.

155
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:36,240
I try to take the stairs instead of
levitating whenever I can. Keep in shape.

156
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:41,540
- Captain!
- We're in hot pursuit. We'll get your friends back.

157
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,720
Uh... the Romulan?

158
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:50,060
He's in our brig. Lana, why was
he still there on Aldebaran III?

159
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:56,020
I think he's a praetorian spy!
Must've infiltrated the dissidents.

160
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:59,440
He fled to the hills after they discovered him.

161
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:05,020
We were the only people at the lab
for weeks. Our paths crossed frequently.

162
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,400
Do you trust him?

163
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,560
About as far as I can throw him.

164
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:12,540
Which -- in your case -- I'd wager is pretty far.

165
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,140
Why didn't you use your abilities
to subdue him?

166
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:26,740
He has tremendous innate powers.
And as I told you, captain... I am
a strict pacifist.

167
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:31,460
I do not utilize my abilities to harm others
unless they pose a direct threat.

168
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:37,080
Bones. Speaking of "direct threats"...
we'll be engaging the Romulan ship soon.

169
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,540
I hope I don't have to call on you, but...

170
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:42,180
If I had a credit for every time you said that.

171
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:46,660
I have the chem lab synthesizing hyronalin.
Best against radiation burns.

172
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,820
SULU ON COMM:
Bridge to captain.

173
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,100
Kirk here. Go ahead, Sulu.

174
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,500
SULU:
The marauder's about to cross
into the Neutral Zone.

175
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:57,600
Sound battle stations. I'm on my way.

176
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,012
How long until the Neutral Zone boundary?

177
00:18:10,013 --> 00:18:11,213
SULU:
Ten seconds.

178
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:15,500
- Lieutenant?
- Our orders recorded and logged, sir.
- Five seconds.

179
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,480
Stay sharp, everyone.

180
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,854
COMPUTER:
Warning -- treaty violation.
Warning -- treaty violation.

181
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,500
Mute that, Uhura.

182
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:29,860
- On course for Romulan space.
- Keep an even hand on the tiller, Sulu.

183
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:37,400
Out of the frying pan... into the fire.

184
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:48,080
Scanning to one-half parsec.

185
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:52,840
There's no sign of the marauder, captain.
She could be cloaked.

186
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:57,540
- I've got something on motion sensors!
- Can we get a phaser lock?

187
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,140
No sir -- but he's out there.

188
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,500
See if you can boost the directional beam.
We need surgical precision.

189
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:05,800
Try to take out his engines without
endangering the habitat module.

190
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:09,360
- Captain, a Romulan ship is
decloaking off our port bow!
- Shields to maximum.

191
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,480
T'liss-class imperial bird-of-prey.
I have wisual.

192
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,459
The marauder?

193
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,636
Negative. The vessel is registered
as the I.R.W. Hawk's Talon.

194
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:29,420
Captain, we're being hailed.

195
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,510
Commander.

196
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:52,240
I received Mr. Spock's message
requesting a parley.

197
00:19:55,680 --> 00:20:01,300
Yet the fact remains: the Enterprise violated
interstellar law by entering Romulan space.

198
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:08,300
Shall we call it "war" now, Captain Kirk?
Or wait for an official declaration?

199
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:18,340
Contacting the Romulans, Spock?
THAT Romulan?

200
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:22,300
On your own initiative? What were you
thinking? Why didn't you ask me?

201
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,400
- You would not have agreed.
- Damn right I wouldn't have agreed!

202
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:30,520
You're lucky I don't rip one of those
stripes right off your sleeve.

203
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:38,140
Captain, I became aware of reports that
Charvanek was granted command of a new
bird-of-prey after she was repatriated.

204
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:45,620
I am confident, once I speak with her,
that she will see the wisdom of assisting
us in pursuing the Romulan dissidents.

205
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:50,680
- She and I have a rapport.
- A "rapport."

206
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,720
Bring her aboard.

207
00:20:59,260 --> 00:20:59,980
Spock.

208
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:07,140
You have 30 minutes. I hope that's
enough time for your... rapport.

209
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:30,180
- Welcome aboard the Enterprise... again.
- Captain.

210
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:34,560
Mr. Dickerson, please conduct the
lieutenant to guest quarters.

211
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,740
Aye, sir.

212
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:58,120
- "Jolan tru."
- And should I greet you as your people would?
"Live long and prosper"?

213
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,020
You may greet me as you wish.

214
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:03,380
Human lore would suggest I offer "the other cheek."

215
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:11,300
I confess... the humans did treat me well.
Still, I was surprised the exchange
was arranged so quickly.

216
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:17,540
Logic dictated that your return would
entice your Praetor to release the
Tellarite merchants held on Remus.

217
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,480
You mean the Tellarite SPIES.

218
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:24,300
They would have sold the information
they acquired. My terminology is apt.

219
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:28,180
Hmm... Now who is being clever, Spock?

220
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:35,110
Your Praetor would seem quite loyal to you.
Is your loyalty to him as great?

221
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:39,640
Commander, he needs your help.

222
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:42,900
I need your help.

223
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:52,960
Your father negotiated the arrangement
that led to my return. The House of Sarek
has my gratitude.

224
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:59,280
I will aid you... if I can.

225
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,340
KIRK:
Commander, I appreciate your assistance.

226
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:09,720
ROMULAN COMMANDER:
Spock mentioned Romulan dissidents and
kidnapped humans with psionic abilities.

227
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:13,180
Our intelligence sources know
nothing of these "marauders."

228
00:23:14,020 --> 00:23:17,880
In order to track them, I will need their
ships' configurations. Armaments.

229
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:20,580
Then we are -- to use an Earth expression -- "in luck."

230
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,940
We apprehended a Romulan commander on Aldebaran III...

231
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:27,940
...an undercover member of the vessel's crew
still loyal to the Praetor.

232
00:23:38,140 --> 00:23:39,960
"Jolan tru."

233
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:45,220
I have never seen this individual before!
He is certainly no Romulan commander.

234
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:47,140
Are you sure?

235
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:55,280
Transporter room, what the hell's going on?!

236
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,340
I beamed the prisoner out of the brig --
just as you ordered, sir.

237
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:01,360
Dammit, chief! I gave no such order!

238
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:07,200
Captain, I know my fleet as well as you
know yours. That man was an imposter!

239
00:24:07,660 --> 00:24:10,580
An imposter... who's now on the loose.

240
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:28,800
Captain, I swear I received orders to transport
the prisoner. I just... I don't know where.

241
00:24:29,180 --> 00:24:34,180
Sir, the targeting scanner's memory logs
have been erased. But the imposter
could not have traveled far.

242
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:38,040
Our shields have been at full power since
Commander Charvanek beamed aboard.

243
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:43,140
- Then he's still on the Enterprise.
- Dickerson, I need security teams on all decks.

244
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:45,220
SCOTT ON COMM:
Intruder alert! Main engineering!

245
00:24:45,660 --> 00:24:46,960
Looks like we found our man.

246
00:24:57,480 --> 00:25:01,770
Sir! The mains are going offline!

247
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:07,180
Hold your fire! He's released
the electro-plasma!

248
00:25:08,380 --> 00:25:09,220
Hand-to-hand!

249
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:12,940
Gotcha, ya lovely.

250
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,020
Clear!

251
00:26:01,660 --> 00:26:06,180
If the nerve pinch was as you described,
Charvanek will be incapacitated for
at least 3 hours.

252
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:10,780
We don't have that kind of time, doctor.
Her second-in-command wants
her returned immediately.

253
00:26:11,020 --> 00:26:13,040
They ARE better equipped to
treat her than we are.

254
00:26:15,260 --> 00:26:19,660
Burke, prepare the commander for transport.
What's HIS status?

255
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:24,600
I'm keeping him under. Pulse 200, blood pressure 20/10.

256
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:29,300
- Romulan or Vulcan, they read the same.
- Vulcan?

257
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,320
The pressure hold he administered.

258
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:35,120
Spock's "Vulcan death grip."

259
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:39,360
McCOY:
Bingo. I've been doing some digging.

260
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:46,620
The Aldebaran colony's last census listed
one Vulcan. A male anthropologist
named Sentek.

261
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:54,780
There's more, Jim. Federation records show
that he's married to our friend Lana.
And his ESP rating is through the roof.

262
00:26:55,420 --> 00:26:59,400
He's got natural psionic abilities way
beyond normal -- even for a Vulcan.

263
00:26:59,800 --> 00:27:03,220
If his powers are already so strong,
why go to an esper lab?

264
00:27:03,940 --> 00:27:05,680
Maybe... to find a mate.

265
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:12,100
A human esper. One that could be uplifted
by the barrier... become his equal.

266
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:15,380
And one who's already embraced
Vulcan philosophy.

267
00:27:15,900 --> 00:27:19,520
Wanna bet Lana's trip into the barrier
wasn't authorized by Starfleet?

268
00:27:27,220 --> 00:27:33,400
To see all the scientists killed...
to have everyone like you taken prisoner.

269
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:36,400
It must have been very difficult.

270
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:48,260
Colleagues, neighbors, friends...
Awful.

271
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:53,120
It's important to allow yourself
time to grieve, Lana.

272
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:56,880
I'd like to try and help if I can.

273
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:06,240
That was a brilliant performance.
We know about you and Sentek.

274
00:28:07,860 --> 00:28:09,300
Why don't you try the TRUTH this time?

275
00:28:09,890 --> 00:28:15,120
- Captain, she's been through a terrible ordeal.
- She scripted the ordeal, counselor!

276
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:18,080
Didn't you, Lana?
You and your husband.

277
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:22,340
He wasn't going to commit suicide
with that disruptor overload at all.

278
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:27,100
He was trying to blow up the lab entrance so
we couldn't find out what REALLY happened.

279
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:38,900
Human evoluton has stalled, captain.

280
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:51,100
A typical man of 2270 -- like you -- is no different
physically from a Cro-Magnon of 100,000 years ago.

281
00:28:54,220 --> 00:28:58,460
But WE are.
We are superior.

282
00:29:00,980 --> 00:29:06,000
I thought you said absolute power
only corrupts selectively.

283
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:11,400
And SELECTION -- whether natural or artificial --
is the engine of evolution.

284
00:29:13,860 --> 00:29:17,140
Your kind should embrace your fate.

285
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:25,060
Instead, you try to control us.
Use us.

286
00:29:33,180 --> 00:29:34,180
Chief.

287
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:47,760
Why do you suppose the Preservers
erected a barrier around our galaxy?

288
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:51,780
Why? Hell, probably to contain us.

289
00:29:52,180 --> 00:29:54,760
To keep violence from spilling
into the universe.

290
00:29:55,960 --> 00:30:01,560
No. It was so that naturally superior
individuals could be uplifted...

291
00:30:01,980 --> 00:30:04,540
...once we had the technology to
venture into the stars.

292
00:30:05,420 --> 00:30:06,920
You don't know what gods think!

293
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:11,460
Yes. I do.

294
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:36,220
SMITH:
Still no sign of the marauder.
He was there... and then he wasn't.

295
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:38,840
Subcommander?

296
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:45,060
Subspace scan completed. We find no
evidence of a cloaked vessel, Enterprise.

297
00:30:46,700 --> 00:30:48,220
The sensor logs you requested.

298
00:30:49,260 --> 00:30:54,380
Our trace of the Romulan kidnappers
disappeared after Sentek lost consciousness
and Lana was put in the brig.

299
00:30:55,580 --> 00:31:00,180
So that's why he tried to disable the power
grid: to prevent us from realizing
the ship was an illusion!

300
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:01,700
TAL:
So it would seem.

301
00:31:07,380 --> 00:31:10,580
Mr. Palmer, run a level 3 diagnostic on
our long-range sensors.

302
00:31:11,180 --> 00:31:13,740
- Let's see how badly they've been compromised.
- Yes sir.

303
00:31:14,780 --> 00:31:22,570
Lt. Sulu... if there is no "Romulan
marauder," then the Enterprise entered
our space without provocation.

304
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:25,520
Starfleet is clearly the aggressor.

305
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:28,120
Subcommander, that's for diplomats
to decide. For now...

306
00:31:28,460 --> 00:31:33,250
For now, you will stand down and
surrender to the Romulan Star Empire!

307
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:38,340
Sir, the bird-of-prey is charging
its plasma weapon!

308
00:31:38,860 --> 00:31:41,825
Captain Kirk to the bridge.

309
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:44,571
Go ahead, Tal. Open fire.

310
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:49,700
And tell your Praetor why you destroyed a
Federation starship instead of capturing it.

311
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,560
Your ship's mission is about to end.
It is scheduled to return to Earth...

312
00:31:54,860 --> 00:31:59,480
...and our sources inform us only 3 other
ships of its class remain in service.

313
00:32:00,500 --> 00:32:03,480
We have no interest in obsolete technology.

314
00:32:05,140 --> 00:32:06,440
"Obsolete"?!

315
00:32:07,860 --> 00:32:13,340
A shame. Unlike you, lieutenant, your
Mr. Spock had an agreeable cunning.

316
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:17,180
May his "katra" find its way to "Vorta Vor."

317
00:32:21,120 --> 00:32:23,180
Evasive maneuvers! Brace for impact!

318
00:32:23,420 --> 00:32:26,880
Romulan weapon reaching
full charge in 3... 2...1...

319
00:32:43,780 --> 00:32:47,000
- Why haven't you fired?!
- Subcommander, I HAVE!

320
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:50,140
Stand aside!

321
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:05,980
Scans show their plasma torpedo
fully charged and operational.

322
00:33:06,700 --> 00:33:10,780
- Why didn't they fire?
- I'm betting they think they did.

323
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:17,120
Subcommander! Power down
our weapons immediately!

324
00:33:17,780 --> 00:33:21,300
Sir. You have recovered sufficiently
to return to duty?

325
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:25,960
The second time you've had to
relinquish command back to me, isn't it?

326
00:33:26,320 --> 00:33:28,020
Your glory is mine, commander.

327
00:33:28,620 --> 00:33:33,340
Tal, we will assist the Enterprise in
its mission. Is that understood?

328
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:36,080
Commander, we have them!
Here in Romulan space!

329
00:33:36,260 --> 00:33:42,600
I have no intention of permitting human
espers -- nor Romulan dissidents -- to attack
the Praetor. Or worse.

330
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:50,500
I suspect there is a greater plan here. A plan
that may jeopardize both the Federation
and our Star Empire.

331
00:33:50,740 --> 00:33:52,900
Your loyalty to the Praetor is admirable.

332
00:33:53,380 --> 00:33:55,910
As, I assume, is yours.

333
00:33:57,560 --> 00:33:59,060
Absolutely, commander.

334
00:34:05,380 --> 00:34:06,300
What's our status?

335
00:34:06,740 --> 00:34:10,480
DRAKE:
Mr. Scott enhanced the forcefield with the ship's
shield grid. Nobody's gonna beam through that.

336
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:13,780
- Indeed. Rather ingenious.
- I'd expect nothing less.

337
00:34:16,460 --> 00:34:20,300
Sulu says you fooled Subcommander Tal into
thinking his weapons malfunctioned.

338
00:34:22,420 --> 00:34:24,180
No need to thank me, captain.

339
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:28,720
Just like you fooled US into thinking
Romulans kidnapped the espers.

340
00:34:30,660 --> 00:34:32,660
Your people STOLE the Halifax, didn't they?

341
00:34:35,320 --> 00:34:37,660
You knew Starfleet would send
another ship to investigate.

342
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:42,400
Sooner or later, we'd track them down. 
So you and Sentek stayed behind --

343
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:49,720
projected that illusion of a marauding vessel --
to buy your compatriots the time they need to
make it to the galactic barrier.

344
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:54,780
Simple humans are so easy to deceive.

345
00:34:55,660 --> 00:34:59,860
They can be tricked into
doing almost anything.

346
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:08,380
Like shutting down their own life support.

347
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:16,820
The Hood. My God... that's
what happened to the Hood!

348
00:35:17,060 --> 00:35:17,640
Why?

349
00:35:18,340 --> 00:35:19,670
Lana, why?

350
00:35:22,420 --> 00:35:24,140
To see if we could.

351
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:34,820
There's nothing you -- or anyone -- can do now.
My brethren will be uplifted by the barrier.

352
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:42,240
Even the great James T. Kirk
will be brought to his knees.

353
00:35:52,500 --> 00:35:56,540
Captain's log, supplemental. What have I done
bringing an esper mutant on board?

354
00:35:57,080 --> 00:35:59,960
I've been exhausted -- but has
my judgment been compromised?

355
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,600
Have I put my ship at unnecessary risk?

356
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:06,400
In the hopes that my senior staff can
provide some insight,

357
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:10,180
I've assembled those who were present
when we first crossed the barrier...

358
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:12,460
...what seems like an eternity ago.

359
00:36:12,980 --> 00:36:16,800
SPOCK:
Ladies and gentlemen, I direct your
attention to stardate 1312.

360
00:36:17,580 --> 00:36:22,700
The so-called "galactic barrier." A field composed
of negative energy surrounding our galaxy.

361
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:24,240
Effectively encasing it.

362
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:27,340
Early in the Enterprise's five-year mission,

363
00:36:28,140 --> 00:36:35,000
I ordered us across the barrier to investigate
the disappearance of an old Earth vessel
some 200 years earlier.

364
00:36:35,720 --> 00:36:37,340
I think we all remember what happened.

365
00:36:37,740 --> 00:36:39,500
Except for those of us that weren't yet aboard.

366
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:45,960
We've read the reports, captain.
Two crewmembers with high ESP ratings
had their abilities altered.

367
00:36:46,890 --> 00:36:50,220
Correction. Their abilities
BOOSTED. Exponentially.

368
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:57,160
So, when the Halifax reaches that barrier
with all of those espers on board...

369
00:36:57,600 --> 00:37:00,080
Counselor, that is precisely
what we must prevent.

370
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:05,340
It is logical that the espers will endeavor
to enter the galactic barrier here,

371
00:37:06,200 --> 00:37:08,260
at the point nearest the Aldebaran system.

372
00:37:08,740 --> 00:37:12,040
The Halifax is a low-warp ship.
That journey would take weeks.

373
00:37:12,360 --> 00:37:16,140
But it's been weeks since they stole the
wessel. What if they already made it?

374
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:23,360
Lt. Smith... As I recall, you were
holding Commander Mitchell's hand
when the crossing occurred.

375
00:37:24,140 --> 00:37:29,380
Any insight you can provide?
Anything unique you may have
experienced via physical contact?

376
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:36,000
Nothing I didn't put in my report, sir.

377
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:40,280
Mr. Spock, defeating one god was hard enough. But a ship full of 'em...!

378
00:37:40,500 --> 00:37:42,620
They're not "gods," Scotty.
They're just humans.

379
00:37:43,680 --> 00:37:47,220
Even with all his power, Gary was still
susceptible to human frailty.

380
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:50,400
Hell, he couldn't even
remember my middle name.

381
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:54,960
Precisely. An uplifted esper's strength
weakens as it is expended.

382
00:37:55,400 --> 00:38:00,380
Then we must use that to our advantage.
Strike first -- before they grow stronger.

383
00:38:00,940 --> 00:38:02,800
We're not out to defeat them, commander.

384
00:38:04,320 --> 00:38:08,670
They're Federation citizens... our brothers,
sisters... even if they are misguided.

385
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,720
Consider this a rescue mission.

386
00:38:14,240 --> 00:38:18,800
PALMER ON COMM:
Captain, transmission from the U.S.S. Kongo.
They've picked up the Halifax's ion trail.

387
00:38:19,120 --> 00:38:22,600
Transfer it to this computer. And tell
Captain Azmi we'll be joining the chase.

388
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:24,960
You heard her. Get to work.

389
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:37,520
Sir, even at maximum sustainable speed,
we can't catch the Halifax before it
enters the barrier.

390
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:38,680
Commander.

391
00:38:43,500 --> 00:38:45,000
What are your ship's warp capabilities?

392
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:50,200
Our birds-of-prey do not utilize what
you refer to as "warp power."

393
00:38:51,140 --> 00:38:53,320
We use other methods to
travel faster than light.

394
00:38:53,860 --> 00:39:00,260
Indeed. There is speculation that Romulans
employ confined quantum singularities
to bend space.

395
00:39:02,180 --> 00:39:03,380
I cannot confirm that.

396
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:08,860
What if a traditional warp field and the fold
from an artificial singularity OVERLAPPED?

397
00:39:11,300 --> 00:39:14,300
A background in astro-sciences comes in
handy when you're a helm officer.

398
00:39:17,900 --> 00:39:22,340
- It may be possible.
- Sulu, you're a genius.

399
00:39:23,120 --> 00:39:24,700
Who am I to argue with you, sir.

400
00:39:25,100 --> 00:39:27,780
Work with Scotty and the Romulan
engineers to enhance our velocity.

401
00:39:30,060 --> 00:39:32,360
Let's see how fast we can
get our girl to go.

402
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:46,320
Lower your deflectors, Enterprise.

403
00:39:47,020 --> 00:39:50,220
- Mr. Chekov?
- Shields down.
- Tractor beam standing by.

404
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:54,040
Activate tractors.
Extend superluminal fold.

405
00:40:07,900 --> 00:40:11,340
Scott to bridge! I've routed the
primary tractor beam through the shuttle bay.

406
00:40:11,580 --> 00:40:14,420
But captain... she's not designed to
take this sort a' strain for long!

407
00:40:14,740 --> 00:40:19,562
You always say that... and she always does.
Mr. Smith?

408
00:40:20,563 --> 00:40:21,533
Punch it.

409
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:23,100
Yes sir!

410
00:40:36,820 --> 00:40:38,420
Six different systems red-lining!

411
00:40:38,700 --> 00:40:40,992
KIRK ON COMM:
Let them red-line!

412
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:43,000
Aye. Me poor bairns.

413
00:41:46,200 --> 00:41:47,620
Well I'll be damned...

414
00:41:54,740 --> 00:41:56,720
Sir, galactic barrier dead ahead.

415
00:41:56,940 --> 00:41:58,800
Signal the Hawk's Talon.
Full stop.

416
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:24,920
As before, sensors and deflectors
yield inexplicable readings.

417
00:42:25,220 --> 00:42:29,240
[OVER COMM] Charvanek to Enterprise.
She's fiercely beautiful, isn't she?

418
00:42:29,660 --> 00:42:32,640
Indeed she is. And deadly

419
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:38,780
- Sir, we're picking up a wessel at the barrier.
- Full mag.

420
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:48,760
Identification confirmed: S.S. Halifax.

421
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:51,720
Ship-to-ship.

422
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:55,460
UHURA:
Hailing frequencies open.

423
00:42:57,240 --> 00:42:59,760
This is Captain James Kirk of the Starship Enterprise.

424
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,520
We are here to render aid.

425
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:08,160
I understand that you have grievances,
and we offer our services

426
00:43:08,600 --> 00:43:10,200
as go-betweens with Starfleet Command.

427
00:43:11,620 --> 00:43:16,560
But it is crucial that you DO NOT
enter the barrier. Please reply.

428
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:28,500
- Uhura, anything?
- Just silence.

429
00:43:32,580 --> 00:43:33,820
There is no one aboard.

430
00:43:35,020 --> 00:43:39,860
Captain, we're detecting another ship nearby.
A starship!

431
00:43:52,200 --> 00:43:58,300
Scanning. It is the Kongo, sir. We are
receiving anomalous readings.

432
00:43:59,000 --> 00:43:59,800
Specify.

433
00:44:00,600 --> 00:44:03,560
It would appear there are only about
two-dozen life forms aboard.

434
00:44:06,240 --> 00:44:08,040
I've tied into the Kongo's bridge, captain.

435
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:09,740
Put it on screen.

436
00:44:39,380 --> 00:44:43,080
You're too late, captain.
Relinquish command...

437
00:44:43,760 --> 00:44:47,560
...or the Enterprise will suffer
the same fate as the Hood!

438
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:22,200
[English subtitles by: Lisa Hansell]

